# Web IDE (`MaldaLang.IDE`)

- Treat this as a **browser learning playground** (Monaco + run/debug/examples).
- Do not implement or document Desktop-only features as if they already exist here (virtual `@malda-section` tabs, MCP config UI, local model browser, UIHost preview, full multi-file project graph).
- Good contributions: Monaco UX, diagnostics presentation, examples browser, learning flows.
- Shared language intelligence lives in `MaldaLang/IDE/LanguageService.cs` — prefer fixing shared logic there when both IDEs should benefit.
- Avoid reintroducing Blazor template scaffold pages (`Counter`, `Weather`, etc.).
